Closes #18709.

Fix bug where `launcherButtonRef` is focused when `Modal` renders, even though it has never even been opened.

Also, add usePreviousValue() hook based on the one in @carbon/ibm-products. 

Side note: I noticed that the `launcherButtonRef` code is disabled when the `enableDialogElement` flag is set to true.  That seems overly optimistic, especially since `launcherButtonRef` currently supports focusing any element, not just the actual launch button. Regardless, that's unrelated to this PR.

#### Changelog

**Changed**

- Fixed Modal logic to only focus launcherButtonRef when the Modal is closed, not when it's initially rendered.

#### Testing / Reviewing

I tested in Storybook after modifying Modal.stories.tsx to add an `input` focus point and a `launcherButtonRef`:

```jsx
export const Default = ({ numberOfButtons, ...args }) => {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  const [popoverOpen, setPopoverOpen] = useState(false);
  const launcherButtonRef = useRef(null);
  return (
    <>
      <input/>
      <Button ref={launcherButtonRef} onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>Launch modal</Button>
      <Modal
        onRequestClose={(e) => {
          action(e);
          setOpen(false);
        }}
        modalHeading="Add a custom domain"
        primaryButtonText="Add"
        secondaryButtonText="Cancel"
        aria-label="Modal content"
        open={open}
        launcherButtonRef={launcherButtonRef}
        {...args}
```

